WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
Two small spheres, both
positively charged,

2
00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.920
are held near each other.

3
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:09.830
Each pushes the other away, with an equal
and opposite force along the line joining

4
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.640
them.

5
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:15.850
For one pair, that force is
tiny: 84 millionths of a newton.

6
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.570
Now slide them together, until the
distance between them is half what it was.

7
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.460
How many times bigger does the force get?

8
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:27.310
In this mission, you'll treat
charged spheres as single points,

9
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.090
and measure the distance
between them the right way.

10
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:34.530
Then you'll find the total force on one
charge when two others push and pull on

11
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.880
it at once.

12
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.620
Your mission: predict how many
times bigger the force gets,

13
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.830
and explain why.
